# CI local, CD remote

To conserve GitHub Actions minutes (we are on **GitHub Free** — see `github-free-plan`), **CI runs on the developer's machine, not in Actions.** GitHub Actions is reserved for **deploys (CD)** and for the few jobs that genuinely cannot run locally.

## The split

- **Local (developer machine)** — lint, format check, typecheck, test, build. Enforced by pre-commit:
  - format/lint on staged files at commit time (existing hooks), and
  - a **`pre-push` hook** that runs the full CI before any push leaves the machine.
- **GitHub Actions** — deploy/release workflows only, plus a minimal build/health gate inside the deploy job so a broken build can't ship. Jobs that can't run locally (CodeQL, secret scanning) stay in Actions on a **schedule**, never per-push.

## Rules for every Wolvrine-owned repo

- **Never** add a `push:` or `pull_request:` trigger to a lint/test/build workflow. Product `ci.yml` is **`workflow_dispatch:`-only** — kept for on-demand runs, but never auto-consumes minutes.
- Every repo has a `ci` script that runs the same checks the old CI did:
  - Node/TS: `"ci": "npm run lint && npm run format:check && npm test && npm run build"` (drop any step the repo genuinely lacks).
  - Python: `ruff check . && ruff format --check . && pytest`.
  - Bun: the `bun run` equivalent of the above.
  - JVM: `mvn verify` / `./gradlew check`.
- Every repo's `.pre-commit-config.yaml` has a `stages: [pre-push]` hook that runs that `ci` command. After cloning, run both `pre-commit install` **and** `pre-commit install --hook-type pre-push`.
- **Deploy workflows stay in Actions** but are **`workflow_dispatch`-only** — no auto-deploy on push (see `ci-internal-deploys`).
- Security/analysis that can't run locally (CodeQL, gitleaks) lives in its **own** workflow on a weekly `schedule:` + `workflow_dispatch:`, never per-push.

## Excluded / special

- `food-delivery-multivendor`, `erp-lite` — excluded from hub tooling standards (see `doc-pack-exclusions`); leave their workflows as-is.
- `The-Street-King` — no CI at all; nothing to change.
- `open-claw-setup/rotate-oci-api-key.yml` — scheduled maintenance, untouchable (see `open-claw-setup-secrets`).

## Supersedes

This supersedes the "Shared CI workflows … called via `workflow_call` from each submodule" decision in [`docs/TOOLING_STANDARDIZATION_PLAN.md`](../docs/TOOLING_STANDARDIZATION_PLAN.md): CI no longer runs in Actions on push/PR. The hub's `lint-test-build-{node,python,bun}.yml` reusable workflows remain callable via `workflow_dispatch` for occasional manual runs, but callers no longer auto-trigger them.
